WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.856 --> 00:00:14.238
Wendy, John, and Michael sailed home.

2
00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:22.124
As they enjoyed the salty ocean breeze and the rolling waves, they imagined their homecoming at Number 14.

3
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:29.530
They pictured their mother's delight, their father's shout of joy, and Nana's leap to embrace them.

4
00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:35.130
In fact, everything in the nursery was already prepared for them.

5
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.433
The beds were made, the window was open, and Mrs.

6
00:00:40.493 --> 00:00:45.195
Darling was waiting—just as she had every day since they had left.

7
00:00:46.236 --> 00:00:51.679
The only change was that between nine in the morning and six at night Nana's dog house was

8
00:00:51.819 --> 00:00:52.940
not in the nursery.

9
00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.782
When the children flew away, Mr.

10
00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.463
Darling felt that he was to blame.

11
00:00:59.484 --> 00:01:02.957
After all, he had chained up Nana and left the children alone.

12
00:01:04.237 --> 00:01:07.338
Nana, he realized, had been the wise one.

13
00:01:08.618 --> 00:01:11.159
If anyone deserved to be locked up, Mr.

14
00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:12.840
Darling decided, it was he.

15
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.481
He crawled into Nana's dog house and wouldn't allow her in.

16
00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:18.941
When Mrs.

17
00:01:18.961 --> 00:01:24.203
Darling begged him to come out, he said, "No, dear, this is where I belong."

18
00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:30.409
He swore that he would never leave the dog house until his children came back.

19
00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.431
Every morning, a taxi came to pick up Mr.

20
00:01:34.451 --> 00:01:37.812
Darling in the dog house and took him to his office.

21
00:01:38.793 --> 00:01:41.454
In the evening, he came home the same way.

22
00:01:42.674 --> 00:01:45.015
Soon the news leaked out to his neighbors.

23
00:01:46.016 --> 00:01:49.277
They were saddened by the Darlings' tragedy and by Mr.

24
00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:50.037
Darling's grief.

25
00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.680
Crowds would follow his taxi home, touched by his devotion.

26
00:01:56.756 --> 00:01:59.298
On the day of the children's return, Mrs.

27
00:01:59.338 --> 00:02:01.940
Darling was in the nursery waiting for her husband.

28
00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.681
She was a very sad woman now.

29
00:02:05.822 --> 00:02:08.944
She had lost her cheerfulness when she lost her children.

30
00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:15.489
The sparkle in the right corner of her mouth, where she kept her secret kiss, had dimmed.

31
00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:22.593
Tearfully she said to Nana, "Last night, I dreamed my little ones had come home."

32
00:02:23.714 --> 00:02:25.575
Nana put her paw gently on Mrs.

33
00:02:25.615 --> 00:02:26.256
Darling's lap.

34
00:02:27.228 --> 00:02:31.031
And there they sat until George was brought home in his dog house.

35
00:02:32.813 --> 00:02:35.015
When he arrived home from work, Mr.

36
00:02:35.035 --> 00:02:36.736
Darling was carried up to the nursery.

37
00:02:38.037 --> 00:02:40.699
He stuck his head out of the dog house to kiss his wife.

38
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:47.585
He sat like that for a while, with his head outside the dog house, talking to Mrs.

39
00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:49.527
Darling and holding her hand.

40
00:02:49.547 --> 00:02:57.193
"I am so full of sadness and regret," he sighed.

41
00:02:58.593 --> 00:03:00.835
Then he curled up in his dog house for a nap.

42
00:03:00.855 --> 00:03:04.877
"Won't you play me something on the piano to put me to sleep?"

43
00:03:05.577 --> 00:03:06.058
he asked.

44
00:03:06.078 --> 00:03:08.819
"And shut the nursery window, dear.

45
00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.760
I feel a chilly draft."

46
00:03:12.421 --> 00:03:14.823
"Oh, George, don't ever ask me to do that!"

47
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:16.004
said Mrs.

48
00:03:16.044 --> 00:03:20.706
Darling. "The window must always be left open for the children."

49
00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:24.068
Mr. Darling apologized, and Mrs.

50
00:03:24.108 --> 00:03:26.450
Darling went into the other room to play the piano.

51
00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.911
Soon he was asleep.

52
00:03:29.952 --> 00:03:34.194
And while he slept, Peter and Tinker Bell flew into the nursery.

53
00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.897
After defeating the pirates, Peter could have returned to his underground home.

54
00:03:41.018 --> 00:03:46.681
He could have stayed there and let Tinker Bell guide Wendy, John, and Michael home—just as he had

55
00:03:46.741 --> 00:03:47.441
first planned.

56
00:03:49.563 --> 00:03:51.724
But Peter had changed his mind.

57
00:03:52.748 --> 00:03:56.491
He sailed on the Jolly Roger because he had come up with a new scheme.

58
00:03:57.852 --> 00:04:01.695
He and Tinker Bell arrived ahead of the others to put his scheme into action.

59
00:04:01.715 --> 00:04:06.499
"Quick, Tink," Peter whispered, "close the window!

60
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.261
Now you and I must hide by the door.

61
00:04:10.242 --> 00:04:14.185
When Wendy flies by, she will think her mother has shut her out forever.

62
00:04:15.246 --> 00:04:17.727
Then she will have to go back to Neverland with me."
